    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66">

                <pb facs="0136" n="116" sameAs="frus:frus1948v01p1/pg116"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB/8–2648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Brazil </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-08-26T18:00:00-04:00">August 26, 1948—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>635. In voting on candidates election UNSC, US has in past supported LA
                    candidates put forward by LA state themselves. Dept has every intention
                    continuing this policy forthcoming GA session. Hope because of current
                    international situation LAs this year will be able present strong candidate
                    which can make substantial contribution to work SC along lines criteria laid
                    down Art. 23 UN Charter. Country like Brazil or Mexico would admirably fill
                    these qualifications.</p>
                <p>Convey substance above FonOff and express hope that in considering problem LA
                    states will bear this factor in mind. Report FonOff reaction. Identical tels
                    sent Rio and Mexico City.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
